# CIPHER — Full Vision Document
> A multiplayer chaos sandbox where the rules change every 30 seconds

---

## Core Concept

CIPHER is a browser-based multiplayer arena game built in Rust + WebAssembly.
Players survive in a shared arena while the community votes on physics and 
gameplay mutations every 30 seconds. No two rounds are ever the same.

The game is named after its creator — ciphrnotfound. The cipher is never 
found because the rules never stay the same long enough to crack.

---

## The Game Loop

```
1. Players join a room (2-8 players)
2. Countdown starts — 3, 2, 1, GO
3. Players survive in the arena (dodge, move, outlast)
4. Every 30 seconds — mutation vote appears
5. Players vote on the next rule change (10 second window)
6. Mutation activates — chaos ensues
7. Last player standing wins the round
8. Scores update — next round begins
9. After 5 rounds — winner declared, lobby resets
```

---

## Arena

The arena is a bounded 2D space rendered on an HTML5 Canvas via WebAssembly.

```
Default arena:
- Square bounds: 800x800 units
- Walls on all four sides
- Floor with friction
- Ceiling (or not, depending on mutation)
- Spawn points in the four corners

Visual style:
- Dark background (#0a0f1e — Astra blue-black)
- Neon player outlines (each player gets a unique color)
- Glowing walls that pulse when mutations activate
- Particle effects on collisions
- Mutation activation: full screen flash + shake
```

---

## Players

Each player is a circle (30px radius default) with:
- Username displayed above
- HP bar (100 default)
- Color unique to their session
- Trail effect showing recent movement path

### Movement
```
Keyboard:   WASD or Arrow Keys
Mouse:      Click to move toward cursor (auto-pathfind)
Both:       Can switch mid-game
```

### Physics (default state)
```
- Gravity: 9.8 downward
- Jump: spacebar, single jump only
- Max speed: 300 units/second
- Friction: 0.85 on ground contact
- Bounce coefficient: 0.3 on wall contact
- Collision: players push each other (no damage on contact)
```

### Elimination
```
- Players are eliminated by falling out of bounds
- Players are eliminated by projectiles (certain mutations)
- Players are eliminated when HP reaches 0
- Eliminated players spectate with free camera
```

---

## Mutation System

The heart of CIPHER. Every 30 seconds a vote appears with 4 options.
Majority wins. Ties are broken randomly.

### Vote UI
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  MUTATION VOTE — 10 seconds             │
│                                         │
│  [A] Gravity flips          — 34%       │
│  [B] Everyone moves 3x      — 28%       │
│  [C] Controls reversed      — 22%       │
│  [D] Arena shrinks          — 16%       │
│                                         │
│  Press A, B, C, or D to vote            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Mutation Categories

#### PHYSICS MUTATIONS
```
gravity_flip        Gravity reverses direction completely
zero_gravity        Gravity disabled — players float freely
heavy_gravity       Gravity 5x stronger — everyone sinks fast
bouncy_world        All surfaces have 0.95 bounce coefficient
sticky_floor        Friction 10x — moving is a struggle
ice_world           Friction 0.01 — nobody can stop sliding
speed_boost         All player max speeds doubled
slow_motion         All physics run at 0.4x speed
giant_players       All player radii triple (90px)
tiny_players        All player radii shrink to 8px
```

#### CONTROL MUTATIONS
```
reversed_controls   Left is right, up is down
inverted_jump       Jump sends you downward
random_keys         WASD randomly remapped every 5 seconds
mouse_only          Keyboard input disabled
keyboard_only       Mouse input disabled  
drift_controls      Input has 0.5 second delay
rotated_controls    Controls rotate 90 degrees clockwise
```

#### ARENA MUTATIONS
```
shrinking_arena     Walls close in 2 units per second
expanding_arena     Walls push out — more space to hide
dark_arena          Visibility radius 150px around each player
tilting_arena       Arena rotates 1 degree per second
floor_is_lava       Bottom wall deals 10 damage per second
portals_active      4 portals appear — entering one exits another
disappearing_floor  Floor tiles randomly disappear every 3 seconds
moving_walls        Walls oscillate in/out at 0.5hz
```

#### PLAYER MUTATIONS
```
invisible_players   All players invisible (names still show)
ghost_mode          Players phase through each other
random_teleport     All players teleport every 15 seconds
hp_drain            Everyone loses 2 HP per second
hp_regen            Everyone gains 1 HP per second
swap_positions      All players swap positions randomly
color_blind         Everyone's color becomes identical gray
clone_mode          Each player spawns a mirrored AI clone
```

#### PROJECTILE MUTATIONS
```
ball_rain           Balls drop from ceiling randomly
bouncy_balls        Indestructible balls spawn and bounce forever
homing_missiles     Slow projectiles that track nearest player
black_holes         3 black holes spawn, pull players in
```

#### CHAOS WILDCARDS (rare — 10% chance to appear in vote)
```
all_mutations       Every active mutation enables simultaneously
mutation_roulette   Random mutation activates every 5 seconds
winner_controls     Round winner picks next mutation manually
reverse_vote        Losing vote activates instead of winning
everything_fine     All mutations disabled — 30 seconds of peace
```

### Mutation Stacking
Mutations stack. After 5 rounds of voting you might have:
- Zero gravity + invisible players + random teleport + ball rain
That combination has never happened before. It will never happen the same way again.

---

## Scoring System

```
Survive 30 seconds:     +10 points
Survive a mutation:     +5 points
Last player standing:   +50 points
Win the round:          +100 points
Voted for winning mutation: +2 points
Most creative death:    Community vote after round — +25 points
```

Leaderboard resets every session. Global leaderboard tracks all-time wins.

---

## Game Modes

### CHAOS (default)
Standard mode. 2-8 players. Mutations every 30 seconds. 5 rounds.

### SPEED RUN
Mutations every 10 seconds instead of 30. For experienced players.
Games last approximately 3 minutes of pure insanity.

### DEMOCRACY
Every mutation vote requires 100% consensus. One player can veto.
Forces negotiation and betrayal. 

### SOLO SURVIVAL
Single player. Mutations chosen randomly by the server.
Survive as many rounds as possible. Global leaderboard.
Share your run with a link — others can watch your replay.

### CIPHER ROYALE
16 players. One giant arena. Mutations every 45 seconds.
Arena shrinks permanently after each mutation regardless of vote.
Last 3 players standing win.

---

## Multiplayer Architecture

```
Client (Rust + WASM):
- Game rendering (Canvas 2D)
- Physics simulation (client-side prediction)
- Input handling
- Vote UI

Server (Rust + Tokio):
- WebSocket connections
- Authoritative game state
- Mutation scheduling
- Vote tallying
- Collision arbitration
- Anti-cheat validation

Protocol:
- Binary serialization (bincode or messagepack)
- 60 tick rate server
- Client interpolation for smooth movement
- State reconciliation on mismatch
```

### Room System
```
Public rooms:    Join any available room instantly
Private rooms:   Create room with 6-character code, share with friends
Spectate:        Watch any public room without playing
Replay:          Every game is recorded, shareable via link
```

