### Color System
```
Background:      #0a0f1e  (deep navy — matches Astra brand)
Arena floor:     #0d1526
Wall default:    #1a2744
Wall mutation:   Pulses with mutation color
Player colors:   8 unique neons — cyan, green, orange, 
                 pink, yellow, purple, red, white
UI text:         #f0f4ff
UI accent:       #2B8EF0  (Astra blue)
Danger:          #ff5f57
Success:         #28c840
Vote A:          #2B8EF0
Vote B:          #28c840  
Vote C:          #febc2e
Vote D:          #ff5f57
```

### Font
```
Headings:  Syne (matches Astra brand)
Game UI:   JetBrains Mono (terminal feel, readable in motion)
```

### Screens

#### Landing / Lobby
```
- Game logo (CIPHER in large Syne font)
- "Play Now" button (instant join public room)
- "Create Private Room" button
- "Solo Survival" button  
- Live count: "847 players online right now"
- Recent chaos feed: "zerogravity + invisibleplayers just activated in Room #4421"
- How to play — 3 bullet points max
```

#### In-Game HUD
```
Top left:     Round X/5 — Timer — Active mutations list
Top center:   Player count remaining
Top right:    Your score — Global position
Bottom:       Mutation vote (when active)
Center:       Arena (full screen)
```

#### Post-Round Screen
```
- Winner announced with animation
- Round stats (who survived longest, craziest death)
- Score update
- "Most creative death" community vote
- 5 second countdown to next round
```

#### End of Game Screen
```
- Final leaderboard
- Highlight reel (best moments auto-clipped)
- Share button — generates link to watch replay
- Play Again / New Room buttons
```

---

## Tech Stack

### Game Engine
```
Rust            Core game logic, physics, mutations
wasm-pack       Compiles Rust to WebAssembly
web-sys         Browser API bindings (Canvas, WebSockets)
```

### Physics
```
rapier2d        2D physics engine — handles collision,
                gravity, forces, joints
                Written in Rust, works perfectly with WASM
```

### Rendering
```
HTML5 Canvas    2D rendering via web-sys
                No heavy WebGL needed for this style
                Smooth 60fps in browser
```

### Multiplayer
```
tokio           Async Rust runtime for server
tokio-tungstenite  WebSocket server
serde + bincode Binary serialization for game state
```

### Frontend Shell
```
React           Lobby, menus, leaderboard, vote UI
Tailwind        Styling
Framer Motion   Mutation activation animations
```

### Backend
```
Rust + Axum     HTTP server for lobby/matchmaking
Redis           Room state, active sessions
PostgreSQL      Persistent leaderboard, replays
```

### Deployment
```
Cloudflare Workers  Edge WebSocket handling
Cloudflare R2       Replay storage
Fly.io              Game server hosting
Vercel              Frontend
```

---

## Viral Mechanics

### Built-in sharing
```
- Every game generates a shareable replay link
- Shareable room codes (6 characters, easy to type)
- "Chaos moment" clips — auto-detect wild mutation combos
  and generate a GIF shareable to X/Twitter
- Leaderboard is public — link your profile
```

### The chaos feed
Public feed on landing page showing real-time mutations happening globally:
```
"Room #8821: zero_gravity + invisible_players + ball_rain just activated"
"Room #4401: ALL MUTATIONS ACTIVE — 6 players remaining"
"Room #2211: democracy mode — players stuck voting for 45 seconds 😭"
```

People will watch this feed just for entertainment.

### Developer credibility
```
- "Built in Rust + WebAssembly" is genuinely impressive
- Post the Rust code on GitHub — developers will star it
- Write a dev blog about compiling Rust to WASM for a game
- That post alone gets you 500+ readers on dev.to
```

---

## Development Phases

### Phase 1 — Solo Playable (Week 1)
```
[ ] Basic arena renders in Canvas via WASM
[ ] Player spawns and moves (keyboard + mouse)
[ ] Basic gravity and collision physics (rapier2d)
[ ] 5 mutations working (gravity_flip, speed_boost, 
    reversed_controls, giant_players, dark_arena)
[ ] Solo survival mode — survive as long as possible
[ ] Death and respawn
[ ] Score counter
```

### Phase 2 — Multiplayer (Week 2)
```
[ ] WebSocket server in Rust
[ ] 2-4 players in same arena
[ ] Client-side prediction
[ ] Server reconciliation
[ ] Room creation and joining
[ ] Player names and colors
```

### Phase 3 — Full Mutation System (Week 3)
```
[ ] All 40+ mutations implemented
[ ] Mutation vote UI
[ ] Vote tallying and activation
[ ] Mutation stacking
[ ] Chaos wildcard mutations
[ ] Visual effects per mutation
```

### Phase 4 — Polish and Ship (Week 4)
```
[ ] Landing page
[ ] All game modes
[ ] Leaderboard
[ ] Replay system
[ ] Shareable links
[ ] Mobile touch support
[ ] Performance optimization
[ ] Deploy to production
```

